{"term":"quarantine","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3e2c5669c8f7be4384","definition":"A period of 40 days, particularly","example":"Now the Question seems to lye thus, where lay the Seeds of the Infection all this while? How came it to stop so long, and not stop any longer? Either the Distemper did not come immediately by Contagion from Body to Body, or if it did, then a Body may be capable to continue infected, without the Disease discovering itself, many Days, nay Weeks together, even not a Quarantine of Days only, but Soixantine, not only 40 Days but 60 Days or longer.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ad01b2b0c3ee0de5e","definition":"A period, instance, or state of isolation from the general public or from native livestock and flora enacted to prevent the spread of any contagious disease.","example":"The tourists were put in quarantine to ensure none of them would be able to spread the plague.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f6bbc1dbdf64db999","definition":"A similar period, instance, or state of rigidly enforced or self-enforced detention or isolation.","example":"Now treating Sandwich seems the fittest choice\nFor Spain, there to condole and to rejoyce:\nHe meets the French, but to avoid all harms,\nSlips into Groine, Embassies bears no Arms.\nThere let him languish a long Quarrentine,\nAnd ne're to England come, till he be clean.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:15d090a2cfd6193930","definition":"A place where such isolation is enforced, a lazaret.","example":"They bring wood, millet, rye, barley, and a little wheat to the quarantine to barter with the Cossaks for salt.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["lazaret","lazaretto","lazar house"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9d143a3ed6d264f256","definition":"A period of time where people are not allowed to leave their homes to contain the spread of an infectious disease.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["lockdown","stay-at-home order"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:df43661803b6e9e3d9","definition":"A blockade of trade, suspension of diplomatic relations, or other action whereby one country seeks to isolate another.","example":"When a great power establishes diplomatic quarantine against them it is well not to go too far on a course on which they appear to be embarking with a light heart.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0e0b76a24e32991ff1","definition":"An isolation of one program, drive, computer, etc. from the rest of a computer network to limit the damage from a bug, computer virus, etc.","example":"Also included is Canary, a ‘quarantine’ program for use as a sample to test for a virus by pairing it with new or suspect programs.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c2dab1b9c884da3143","definition":"The program, drive, computer, etc. thus isolated.","example":"If they click on the link then they're added to your approved senders list and their message is moved to your inbox; if they don't, the message stays in quarantine.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"countable, figuratively, uncountable","wordFamily":["community quarantine","free quarantine","K-Quarantine","nonquarantine","prequarantine","quaranteam","quarantine-breaking","quarantinee","quarantine flag","quarantine ground","quarantine kennel","quarantine officer","quarantine station","quarantini","quarantinism","quarantinist","queerantine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarantine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:52b40f65b612b1c00b","definition":"To place into isolation to prevent the spread of any contagious disease.","example":"Venice began quarantining incoming ships for 40 days in 1448 to prevent further outbreaks of bubonic plague.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily"